26-06-18T15:36:25Z","closed_at":"2026-06-18T15:25:20Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in **Linux**:\n- v4.7.beta3.mono.official [860821708]\n- v4.7.beta1.mono.official [1c8cc9e7e]\n\nNot reproducible in **Linux**:\n- v4.7.dev5.mono.official [a8643700c]\n\nNot reproducible in **Windows**:\n- v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n- v4.7.beta3.official [860821708] \n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta3.mono - Fedora Linux 44 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9060 XT (RADV GFX1200) - AMD Ryzen 7 9700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 30.48 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI made a release build of my game and noticed a lot of errors on console. These error messages are not displayed when the game is run from Godot editor, they are displayed only when release executable is run from console. Errors are printed when bullet hits the wall and is destroyed. Error message was about tilemap layer and tree_entered/tree_exiting connections, which didn't make any sense as the only way bullets and that tilemap layer are connected is the collisions physics.\n\nSo here is an MRP, which:\n1. launches bullets (Node2D + Sprite2D + Area2D + CollisionShape2D)\n1. bullet collides to a wall (StaticBody2D + CollisionShape2D)\n1. bullet's Area2D/body_entered signal is emitted\n1. bullet handles the signal by queue freeing itself\n\n<img width=\"580\" height=\"258\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d3071bc2-c20b-420f-bb8b-62951bfb0c38\" />\n\n-> no errors in Godot editor \n-> BUG: when the release version is run, every time a bullet is freed, errors are printed:\n\n```\nBULLET HIT WALL!\nERROR: Attempt to disconnect a nonexistent connection from 'StaticBody2D:<StaticBody2D#32715572594>'. Signal: 'tree_entered', callable: ''.\n   at: _disconnect (core/object/object.cpp:1643)\nERROR: Attempt to disconnect a nonexistent connection from 'StaticBody2D:<StaticBody2D#32715572594>'. Signal: 'tree_exiting', callable: ''.\n   at: _disconnect (core/object/object.cpp:1643)\n```\n\n<img width=\"1127\" height=\"255\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd895ae4-44ed-42b4-b2d8-932f58dc220f\" />\n\nDespite of the errors everything seems to work as expected. But I would guess that the performance cost of the internal error handling is not zero, so in a bullet-heavy game I really would like to get rid of these kind of things.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the MRP.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[collision-free-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28226898/collision-free-test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119740/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119740/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}